Spec: Authenticated Agent control endpoint

Purpose:
  Expose exact-scope lease acquisition and separate owner administration over actual device-authenticated TLS.

Owns:
  ./control_server.go
  ./control_server_test.go

Must:
  Derive the caller from verified TLS state, bind visitor lease requests to that device and recheck current role on every request.
  Return a current lease authority snapshot to the authenticated visitor on acquisition, or to its publishing device after signature, scope, version and expiry validation.
  Bind the server certificate key and owner root to persistent authority before serving; bound leases by certificate expiry as well as `120` seconds.
  Keep owner mutations separate from ordinary Agent requests, compare expected versions and retain original operation IDs without automatic replay.
  Enforce exact JSON fields, `64` KiB bodies, bounded headers/timeouts, at most `8` concurrent calls per device and `32` globally.
  Expose fixed correlated errors only; never log raw control requests, tokens, certificates or network addresses.
  Keep new control networking local to explicit listener ownership; do not deploy or change legacy ECS listeners.
  Check up to sixty-four current lease snapshots per authenticated batch, bound each scope to the actual visitor or publisher and return only aligned validity plus server epoch.
